WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.120
"Natural Dietary Remedy for Insomnia"

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.280
There is a perception that time
spent asleep is time wasted,

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.400
but it is widely recognized that
inadequate sleep is associated

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.040
with multiple acute
and chronic conditions,

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.160
and results in the increased
risk of death and disease.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.920
Force people to go one week with
only six hours of sleep a night,

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.760
and you can change expression
of more than 700 genes.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.520
The most dire effect may
be endothelial dysfunction.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.520
The endothelium is the thin layer of
cells that covers the internal surface

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.560
of blood vessels and is responsible
for allowing our arteries

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.880
to relax and dilate
back open properly.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.480
Randomize people for about a week
to get five rather than seven hours

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.600
of sleep, and just that two-hour
difference a night resulted

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.680
in a significant impairment
in artery function.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.480
Okay, but what do these numbers mean?
How bad is a week of 5-hour nights?

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.360
Sleep deprivation is no joke.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.680
The magnitude of impairment is similar
to that reported in people who smoke,

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.720
have diabetes, or have
coronary artery disease.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.080
No wonder people who sleep less than
seven hours a night may experience

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.600
a 12% to 35% increased
risk of premature death

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.240
compared to those who
get a full seven hours.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.720
Yet a significant proportion
of the population may

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.280
routinely get less than that.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.560
Sufficiently long, restful
sleep sessions each night

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:35.600
are said to be an indisputable
cornerstone of good health.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.840
Okay, so what can we do about it?

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.600
Those who have sleep apnea,
a common consequence of obesity

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.520
that interferes with sleep, benefit
from the use of CPAP machines

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.865
while they're losing the weight to treat
the underlying cause, hopefully.

00:01:48.865 --> 00:01:52.540
But what if apnea isn't your problem?

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.760
What if you just have trouble
falling asleep or staying asleep?

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.080
In my book How Not to Diet, I have a
whole section on sleep enhancement,

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.080
where I go through the Four
Rules of Sleep Conditioning

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.720
and the Four Rules
of Sleep Hygiene.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.240
What if you follow those guidelines
but still can't get to sleep?

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.800
Any natural dietary remedies?
I already have videos on using

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.880
kiwifruit to fight insomnia,
and tart cherries, too.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.600
Are there any vegetables
that might help?

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.920
Lactuca sativa is a plant that
has been traditionally used

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.920
in the treatment of insomnia.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.800
What is this exotic sounding
leafy vegetable? Lettuce!

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:35.120
Evidently lettuce extracts have been
used from the time of the Roman Empire

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.440
as agents with sedative and
sleep-inducing properties.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.360
Lettuce actually does have a hypnotic
substance in it called lactucin,

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:46.320
which is what makes
lettuce taste a little bitter.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.240
But you don't know if it actually
works until you put it to the test.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:56.000
And it works...in toads.
But it also works in rodents.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.280
Sleep in both mice and rats
is enhanced by romaine lettuce.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.880
They used romaine since
it has a higher lactucin content

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:08.160
compared to other lettuces.
Okay, but does it work in people?

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.760
About 10 years ago, a study was
published in which insomnia sufferers

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.120
were randomized to receive lettuce seed
oil, oil extracted from lettuce seeds.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.240
Within a week, about 70% of those
in the lettuce seed oil group

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.640
said their insomnia very much
or much improved,

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.600
compared to only 20% in
the placebo control group.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:29.360
The researchers concluded that lettuce
seed oil was found to be a useful,

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:34.000
safe sleeping aid in geriatric patients
suffering from sleeping difficulties.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.680
They chose to study older individuals
because insomnia affects surprisingly

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.880
20 to 40% of older adults
at least a few nights a month.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:46.240
You think that's bad. Sleep
disturbances can plague as many

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.080
as nearly 8 out of 10 women
during pregnancy.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.480
Of course, there's lots
of different sleeping pills,

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.520
but they may endanger
the fetus or mother.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:59.040
For example, doctors frequently
prescribe Ambien for pregnant women

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.400
who have trouble sleeping, but Ambien
use is associated with a wide range

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.480
of adverse pregnancy outcomes

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.480
like low birth weight babies,
premature birth, and cesarean section.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.960
And the use of valium during
pregnancy has been linked

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.040
to birth defects
including limb deficiencies.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:21.280
There has to be a better way.
What about trying lettuce?

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.680
The lettuce oil study had
a number of limitations.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.960
For example, it was only single-blind,
meaning the researchers knew

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.760
who was on the lettuce supplements
and who was on placebo,

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:33.360
which could have introduced some bias.
But the researchers essentially said,

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.120
"Give us a break. Big pharma
has billions to spend on research.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.080
No one wants to fund
studies on lettuce."

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.120
Finally, we got a double-blind,
placebo-controlled study,

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.760
but this time on a whole food,
not just a lettuce seed extract.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.720
Yeah, but how do you come
up with a placebo lettuce?

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.610
How are you going to hide who 
gets lettuce and who doesn't?

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:56.640
Well, you can't fit a head
of lettuce into a capsule,

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:00.240
but you can fit whole lettuce seeds.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:03.920
And here we go: a double-blind
randomized placebo-controlled trial

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.760
on lettuce seeds for
pregnancy-related insomnia.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.480
A hundred pregnant women
with insomnia were randomized

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.600
to receive capsules containing
either a quarter teaspoon

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:16.800
of ground lettuce seeds or
a placebo for two weeks,

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.840
and those on the lettuce seeds
saw a significant improvement

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.680
in a sleep quality index score

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:26.026
compared to placebo
with no reported side effects.

